{"id":"ed01e9bd-92e8-4e08-9d20-b6bec50beedb","object":"chat.completion","created":1793329800,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Read the remaining logger regions and check environ imports.\n\n```python\nprint(read_range(\"deepinfer/logger.py\", 66, 115)['content'])\nprint(read_range(\"deepinfer/environ.py\", 1, 17)['content'])\n```","reasoning_content":"The environ.py edit is already done (config added, helper `_int_or_none_min` added). Let me verify it compiles and then edit logger.py.\n\nI need to write logger.py changes: NewLineFormatter with max_message_chars keyword-only, truncation, and _setup_logger reading envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS.\n\nLet me look at the format method more carefully. `record.message` is set by super().format(). I need to truncate the message before formatting, but must not mutate the record. Approach:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    max_chars = self.max_message_chars\n    if max_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n        # compute message with args substituted\n        ...\n```\n\nImportant: the message must be args-substituted first. `record.getMessage()` does `msg % args`. We need to not modify record. So:\n\n```python\nmessage = record.getMessage()\nif len(message) > max_chars:\n    truncated = _truncate(message, max_chars)\n    record_copy = copy.copy(record)  # shallow copy\n    record_copy.msg = truncated\n    record_copy.args = None\n    record = record_copy\n```\n\nBut careful: copy.copy of LogRecord — `logging.LogRecord` supports `__dict__` copy; copy.copy should work. However record.message might be cached attribute in __dict__; we need to delete it. Also the formatter uses `record.message` in format() for multiline prefix computation.\n\nAlternative approach avoiding copying: compute the formatted string manually? Simpler: use a shallow copy and del copy.message if present.\n\nActually simpler: since super().format(record) computes `record.message = record.getMessage()`, we can do it manually:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    message = record.getMessage()\n    if limit exceeded:\n        record = _copy_record_with_message(record, truncated)\n    msg = super().format(record)\n    ...\n```\n\nWhere the copy: `import copy` — but allowed imports list only includes standard modules for action code; logger.py can import anything (it's file content, not action code). Fine.\n\nAlso careful with exception info: copy retains exc_info and stack_info; super().format appends them. Good.\n\nNote: for the message with args substitution, record.getMessage can raise if args mismatch... original behavior would raise too in format(). Fine.\n\nEdge: if record.msg is not a str... getMessage() handles.\n\nNow the multiline prefix logic: `if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message`. With the copied record, record.message gets set by super().format(). Fine.\n\nTruncation function:\n\n```python\n_TRUNCATION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\nMARKER_LEN = 15\n```\n\nCheck: \"...<omitted>...\" is 3 + 9 + 3 = 15. Yes, \"<omitted>\" is 9 chars.\n\nremaining = budget - 15; head = (remaining + 1) // 2 (ceil half), tail = remaining - head. For budget 32: remaining=17, head=9, tail=8. ✓\n\nSo head = (remaining + 1) // 2 gives ceil(17/2)=9. Good. tail = remaining - head = 8.\n\nThen message[:head] + marker + message[-tail:] (if tail > 0 else message[:head]+marker).\n\nValidation in __init__:\n\n```python\nif max_message_chars is not None:\n    if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int) or max_message_chars < 32:\n        raise ValueError(...)\n```\n\nAlso validation: must be int; other values raise ValueError.\n\n_setup_logger: `fmt = NewLineFormatter(_FORMAT, datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT, use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(), max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS)`. Need import: `from deepinfer.environ import envs` — check if logger.py already imports environ. Fr